	(footprint "o2-probe:SGX-OX-ROHS-Mini_ISS2"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "21b60f91-e0b4-5aae-a6a9-ae77d6cfb7d5")
		(at 110 127.5)
		(descr "SGX-OX-ROHS-Mini footprint: body dia 14.40, height 8.30, three dia 0.64 pins at 2.54 pitch, pin length 4.0, pin-row offset 2.50, general tolerance +/-0.15 mm. pinmap: DS-0637-SGX-OX-ROHS-Mini Issue 2 (28-May-2026), the Product Dimensions figure on PDF page 2 (the sheet numbered Page 1/1), read 2026-09-01 at 1400 dpi. Issue 1 (07-Apr-2025) page 2 carries the same figure and agrees on every dimension above and on pin identity, so the two issues do not conflict. view: BOTTOM. The figure is the pin-face view, placed under the pins-down side view and showing the three pins end-on, so the F.Cu top view is its mirror. leaders: traced one at a time to their arrowheads, not read as a list. The Counter leader lands on the LEFT pin, Working on the CENTRE pin and Reference on the RIGHT pin, giving Counter, Working, Reference left to right in this BOTTOM view and Reference, Working, Counter left to right in the F.Cu top view; the centre pin is Working. Tracing is required because the two right-hand labels are stacked Reference above Working while their leaders land on the right and centre pins, so the stacked label order is not the pin order. This footprint places pad 1 (CE) at x=-2.54, pad 3 (WE) at x=0 and pad 2 (RE) at x=+2.54, the 180-degree insertion, which keeps CELL_RE closest to U7.13. The page 1 prose ordering 'Counter, Reference and Working' is NOT the physical pin order and must not be used. socket: the cell may NOT be soldered (DS-0317 Issue 2 note 3, the same-platform 4-series sheet: 'Do not glue or solder to the connector pins ... please use PCB sockets'), so the three holes take a receptacle, not the pin. Drill 1.32 is TE Connectivity 5050462 (customer drawing C-5050462 rev P: recommended hole 1.32 +0.10/-0.00 hand insertion, accepts 0.36-0.66 mm pins, 4.19 mm max pin length against this cell's 4.0 mm pin, 2.54 mm min contact point). The 2.0 mm land is deliberately oversized so the same board can be bored to 1.40 and take Cambion 450-3703 instead (TDS 19-Aug-2025: for .025 (0,64) pins, hole 1.40, flange dia 1.88, 3.61 mm below the flange): at 1.32 the annular ring is 0.34 mm and at 1.40 it is 0.30 mm, and the land still covers the TE 1.78 and Cambion 1.88 flanges. The gasward-offset 3 x 6 mm oblong NPTH includes the sensor axis and provides lateral rear-port flow without relying on the undimensioned port diameter.")
		(tags "SGX oxygen electrochemical DS-0637 Issue 1 pinout-verified")
		(property "Reference" "U11"
