		(property "Design Note" "Negative-injection clamp on PA6. Pin 1 is the CATHODE and goes to VIN_MON; pin 2 is the ANODE and goes to AGND. It therefore sits reverse-biased at +1.2 V in normal operation and conducts only when the pin is pulled below ground. See the block comment above for the Table 50 rating, the part-class argument against the 1N4148W, the leakage budget, and the 2026-09-12 correction of both the polarity and the package"
