		(property "Design Note" "3V3A rail monitor divider bottom leg; see R24. 47k -> 27k on 2026-09-12 because the ADC full scale became 2.500 V when VREF+ moved to /VREF_TRIM. Ratio 27/74 = 0.3649, so 3.3 V reads 1.204 V and the CEILING RISES to 6.85 V -- BETTER than the 6.60 V this divider had against a 3.3 V full scale, so the rail keeps its over-range headroom rather than losing it. Source impedance also falls 23.5k -> 17.2k, further inside Table 59's 50k. FIRMWARE follows automatically: gen_hw_contract.py derives O2P_HW_DIV_VA_NUM/DEN from these two values"
			(at 0 0 90)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "4b0b7da7-d2e9-5d14-bd7f-df54fde6b703")
			(effects
